1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,231
Bank reconciliation proves that the bank
account in

2
00:00:03,231 --> 00:00:06,058
Miftah agrees with the bank's own
statement.

3
00:00:06,058 --> 00:00:09,289
Open Accounting and, under Bank, choose
Bank reconciliation.

4
00:00:09,289 --> 00:00:13,732
Each bank account is listed with its
ledger account, and the

5
00:00:13,732 --> 00:00:17,771
bank's TRN is already on file for Palm
Ridge Residences.

6
00:00:17,771 --> 00:00:21,810
Choose Import statement and pick the
August 2026 statement file.

7
00:00:21,810 --> 00:00:24,637
Miftah recognises the columns: date,
description, reference,

8
00:00:24,637 --> 00:00:27,060
cheque number, debit, credit and balance.

9
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:31,503
Save the mapping, and next month's file
imports in one step.

10
00:00:31,503 --> 00:00:35,542
The preview reads the opening balance,
585,587.81, and the closing

11
00:00:35,542 --> 00:00:39,581
balance, 622,895.31, from the file, and
finds six new lines.

12
00:00:39,581 --> 00:00:40,389
Import them.

13
00:00:40,389 --> 00:00:43,216
Now open the workspace: the statement on

14
00:00:43,216 --> 00:00:46,043
the left, the books on the right.

15
00:00:46,043 --> 00:00:46,851
Select Auto-match.

16
00:00:46,851 --> 00:00:49,678
The three cheque clearings find their
cheques

17
00:00:49,678 --> 00:00:52,102
by cheque number, with high confidence.

18
00:00:52,102 --> 00:00:53,313
Confirm all high.

19
00:00:53,313 --> 00:00:57,756
Three lines are left, because only the
bank knew about them.

20
00:00:57,756 --> 00:01:01,391
The first is the account maintenance
charge of 105.

21
00:01:01,391 --> 00:01:04,622
Record it from the line as a bank

22
00:01:04,622 --> 00:01:07,853
charge, and tick that the amount includes
VAT.

23
00:01:07,853 --> 00:01:11,488
Because the bank's TRN is on file, the
journal

24
00:01:11,488 --> 00:01:14,719
debits the charge with 100 and Input VAT

25
00:01:14,719 --> 00:01:17,950
with 5, and credits the bank with 105.

26
00:01:17,950 --> 00:01:18,758
Book it.

27
00:01:18,758 --> 00:01:21,989
The profit credit of 412.50 is booked as

28
00:01:21,989 --> 00:01:24,816
interest: debit the bank, credit Bank
interest.

29
00:01:24,816 --> 00:01:28,855
The inward transfer of 2,500 has not been
identified yet.

30
00:01:28,855 --> 00:01:31,279
Book it as an unidentified receipt.

31
00:01:31,279 --> 00:01:36,125
The bank is debited and Unidentified bank
receipts is credited, until the

32
00:01:36,125 --> 00:01:40,568
tenant is found and the money is received
against their instalment.

33
00:01:40,568 --> 00:01:41,780
Now reconcile August.

34
00:01:41,780 --> 00:01:45,011
Enter the period, the first to the
thirty-first

35
00:01:45,011 --> 00:01:47,838
of August, and start the first
reconciliation.

36
00:01:47,838 --> 00:01:51,473
The statement and the books both read
622,895.31, nothing

37
00:01:51,473 --> 00:01:54,704
is in transit, and the difference is zero.

38
00:01:54,704 --> 00:01:57,127
Every check passes, so select Finalize.

39
00:01:57,127 --> 00:02:01,166
Finalising locks this bank account through
31 August, so no

40
00:02:01,166 --> 00:02:04,801
entry can change a month you have signed
off.

41
00:02:04,801 --> 00:02:09,648
The reconciliation report is ready as a
PDF, in English or Arabic.
